#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-SEND-0119 expect=violation domain=CO
#note "The OTHER arm: the series is CONTIGUOUS so the gap test passes, then the min_length test flags COVAL because suffix 0 is not the terminal member (hi is 1) and its declared length 100 is below min_length 200. Pins that the 200-character split is judged from the DECLARED WIDTH. M3-D22 moved this rule's Executability from 'Fully Executable' to 'Partially Executable - Possible Underreporting' with no Check change: column_series_metadata reads only DECLARED column lengths and never a data cell, so the sheet's Condition ('Comment value > 200 characters in length') cannot be detected on an unsplit comment. Reading the data would need a length-of-value operator the engine does not have. Rule round 2026-10-12 (owner; CENSUS-ov-display-class): the finding names its subject, the COVAL series as present ($coval_series = [COVAL, COVAL1]), instead of the authored COVAL entry, which a dataset finding lists by name only."
#library standard=sendig version=3-1-1
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=1 "$coval_series"="[COVAL, COVAL1]"
dataset CO label="Comments"
col STUDYID type=Char length=12 label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char length=2  label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char length=20 label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col COSEQ   type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col COVAL   type=Char length=100 label="Comment"
col COVAL1  type=Char length=200 label="Comment Part 1"
---
S1 | CO | 001 | 1 | A short first chunk | the continuation
S1 | CO | 002 | 1 | Second comment | its continuation
---
